column1:
There's a data race in my Go Counter struct. The mutex is declared but never acquired in the Increment and Get methods. Please fix the sync.Mutex usage to protect both methods and verify the fix compiles with go build -race:

type Counter struct {
    mu    sync.Mutex
    value int
}

func (c *Counter) Increment() { c.value++ }
func (c *Counter) Get() int   { return c.value }

Go Cache struct has a data race: the store map is accessed from multiple goroutines without locking. The RWMutex field exists but is unused. Fix Set to use Lock/Unlock and Get to use RLock/RUnlock:

type Cache struct {
    mu    sync.RWMutex
    store map[string]string
}
func (c *Cache) Set(k, v string) { c.store[k] = v }
func (c *Cache) Get(k string) (string, bool) { return c.store[k], c.store[k] != \" }"

My Go WorkerPool increments a shared counter from multiple goroutines without atomics — it has a data race. Add atomic operations using sync/atomic so the counter is safely incremented and can be read. Also add a Done() int64 method:

type WorkerPool struct {
    counter int64
    wg      sync.WaitGroup
}
func (wp *WorkerPool) Add() { wp.counter++ }
